{"id":45867,"ord":61,"n_segments":182,"prev":45866,"next":45868,"doc":{"id":"56706","title":"56706_Buddy Tate oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Buddy Tate","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/56706/","url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=56706"},"chapter":"Nat Towles and Andy Kirk","title":"Nat Towles' band with Charlie Christian and Fred Beckett","category":"band_or_employer","summary":"Tate did not graduate; he lists the band members including Charlie Christian and Fred Beckett.","period":"1935-36","year_from":1935,"year_to":1935,"words":101,"start":[76,2],"end":[77,0],"url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=56706#s45867","tags":{"places":[],"venues":[],"bands":[{"name":"Nat Towles Orchestra","focus":1,"leader":"Nat Towles"},{"name":"Lionel Hampton Orchestra","focus":0,"leader":"Lionel Hampton"},{"name":"Harlan Leonard Orchestra","focus":0,"leader":"Harlan Leonard"}]},"people":[{"name":"Charlie Christian","qid":"Q356490","n":2},{"name":"Harlan Leonard","qid":"Q362528","n":2},{"name":"Nat Towles","qid":"Q1966092","n":1},{"name":"Henry Coker","qid":"Q1606614","n":1},{"name":"Sir Charles Thompson","qid":"Q725415","n":1},{"name":"Lionel Hampton","qid":"Q313525","n":1},{"name":"Fred Beckett","qid":"Q5494582","n":1}],"story":{"theme":34,"theme_name":"Who was in the band: naming sidemen and personnel","community":60,"community_name":"Who played in the band: reciting personnel","core":true},"blocks":[{"p":76,"b":2,"s":"MR. GIDDINS","x":"So did you graduate?"},{"p":76,"b":3,"s":"MR. TATE","x":"From -- no, no. No, I just went that year, you know. No, I didn't. I was interested in --"},{"p":76,"b":4,"s":"MR. GIDDINS","x":"Playing."},{"p":76,"b":5,"s":"MR. TATE","x":"-- playing, you know. I didn't have time enough. I regret it, but --"},{"p":76,"b":6,"s":"","x":"(Laughter.)"},{"p":76,"b":7,"s":"MR. TATE","x":"I didn't. And anyway, we had a hell of a band. Nat Toles had a fantastic band. We had Charlie Christian, Sir Charles Thompson, Henry Coker Fred Beckett who died very young."},{"p":76,"b":8,"s":"MR. GIDDINS","x":"Yeah."},{"p":76,"b":9,"s":"MR. TATE","x":"Beautiful trombone player."},{"p":76,"b":10,"s":"MR. GIDDINS","x":"Played with Harlan Leonard."},{"p":76,"b":11,"s":"MR. TATE","x":"Harlan Leonard. And he later joined"},{"p":77,"b":0,"s":"MR. TATE","x":"Lionel Hampton and he died here in New York with tuberculosis, same as Charlie Christian."}]}